 "summary": "Nothing in TauCeti already provides the primitive Dirichlet \u2194 ray class bundle equivalence, the weight formula at all nonzero ideals, the coprimality-by-norm criterion for `ratModulus`, or the \u211a-specific Hecke/Dirichlet L-function comparison; the existing `onIdeals_ratDirichletEquiv_symm` covers only ideals prime to the modulus and is reused. The proofs build on existing API (`ratDirichletEquiv_induced`, `PrimitiveRayClassCharacter.of_eq_iff`, `dvd_ratModulus_absNorm`, the degree-one normCoeff and absNorm lemmas, `LSeries_congr`, `meromorphicContinuation_eq_toMeromorphicNFOn`).",
